{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "An Emotional Week", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Rest and Relaxation", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe ways of solving problems and getting things done in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking Hypothetically About the Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to talk about things that were possible in the past and may or may not have happened. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The structure: <br/><br/><span class=\"strong\"> Subject + modal verb + have + verb  (past participle)</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I             could              have        done<br/> You             should              have        made<br/> She            would               have        said</span><br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> to talk about  the possibilities of how something in the past could have been different.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I could have used this information earlier.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> to talk about past events that did not happen and to speculate about events that may or may not have happened.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">We should have made a reservation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to speculate negatively about what may or may not have happened.<br/> You also use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to express regret for past actions.<br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to express and imagine how a result might have been different in the past.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I  would have gotten a facial. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "* <span class=\"italic\">Would have</span> is used when we are more certain about a result than <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I could have used this information earlier.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It would have been great to be aware of ways to improve communication with people. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We should have made a reservation. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You could have gotten a massage and pedicure.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I would have gotten a facial.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "What Clauses and Long Noun Phrases as Subjects", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You shift emphasis from the beginning to another part of the sentence by using <span class=\"italic\">what</span>, <span class=\"italic\">that</span> and <span class=\"italic\">who</span> phrases as subjects.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, you focus on the subject - that is the person or thing that is doing the action. <br/>  Example: <span class=\"italic\">Joan told a hilarious joke.</span><br/>(Joan does the action.)<br/><br/> When you want to emphasize a different part of the sentence, you isolate that part and we put the rest of the information into a <span class=\"italic\">what</span>-phrase (or a <span class=\"italic\">that</span>-clause.)<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">What was hilarious, was the joke Joan told.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">That</span> with the subject from the original sentence becomes the subordinated content clause.<br/> Example: <span class=\"italic\">That she imitated our teacher was funny.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">What</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Who</span> begins the noun phrase. The effect is that more emphasis is placed on the information at the end of the sentence.<br/> Example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">What was hilarious was her imitation of the teacher.</span><br/>        <span class=\"italic\"> Who she should have made fun of was the principal.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "That we both managed to get through some difficult situations is amazing!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What's important is that we learned something from our experiences.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What's frustrating is that apparently not many people seem interested in working on this part of their personalities.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "What would be great would be to spend the day immersed in luxury in a spa.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "drained", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very tired", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm drained from an emotional week!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to gauge", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a judgement about", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We both learned that we need to use our emotional intelligence to gauge others' emotional states and then react appropriately. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "aware", "type": "name"}, {"content": "knowing that something exists", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Yes, it would have been great to be aware of ways to improve communication with people. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "apparently", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to describe something that appears to be true based on what is known", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What's frustrating is that apparently not many people seem interested in working on this part of their personalities.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "immersed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to fully involve yourself in an activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What would be great would be to spend the day immersed in luxury in a spa.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "disappointed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the state of feeling sad, unhappy about or displeased with something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Now I'm disappointed that we didn't think of this sooner.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn9le04ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "I can't wait", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be very excited about a future event", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't wait for our next adventure!", "type": "example"}, {"conten